    "text": "A point charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is situated at a distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> from one end of a thin non-conducting rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> having a charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> (uniformly distributed along its length) as shown in fig. Then the magnitude of the electric force between them is:<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0032_dde292d5b0a2.png\" style=\"width:3.10694in;height:0.74653in\" />"
  },
